The subdirectory 'testocc' contains a variant of the 1D SHF package
which contains the option to run an occupation constraint calculation.
Only three file which contain reevant modifications are contained as
such. All other files are linked to the mother code in 'source_1D'.

To compile and link issue './clocc' for Intel Fortran or './clocc_g77'
for GNU Fortran while being in the base directory. This produces the
executable 'hafotest.exe'.

The input file contains a new line at the end which reads the number
of the contraint state in the level sequence of the code and the
wanted occupation (between 0 and 1) for that state. For an example
see the batch file 'scanv2.bat' in the subrdirctory 'test'.

